From fc47c8efeba070256e4e53227d5bd7b6c9c2e92e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:02:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/21] anv/bvh: size parent_child_count_map per block, not per
 internal node

encode.comp writes parent_child_count_map[bvh_block_offset] and
update.comp reads it by the parent's block index. Internal nodes and leaves
share the block numbering, so the index goes up to internal + leaf blocks,
but the map was sized for internal_count entries: every BLAS built with
ALLOW_UPDATE wrote up to leaf_count bytes past the size reported by
vkGetAccelerationStructureBuildSizesKHR.

D3D12 apps (vkd3d-proton) pack acceleration structures back to back, so
the overrun lands on the next AS header. In Cyberpunk 2077 a per-frame
ALLOW_UPDATE BLAS rebuild left the neighbour's copy_dispatch_size
inconsistent with its compacted_size; that field drives the indirect
dispatch of the compaction copy, and the GPU hangs seen when loading with
RT on were in copy.comp on the render queue.

Size it like parent_child_map (one entry per block).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream 4f554dafa8d sized it as internal + leaf; this keeps the extra
entry that parent_child_map also has.

(cherry picked from commit 5206a28dab8d206c81a4fc79c448d60a9b3778d4)
Upstream 4f554dafa8d sized it as internal + leaf; this keeps the extra
entry that parent_child_map also has.

(cherry picked from commit 5596e6061e3c792acc20eeef70511a9abe4743e5)
---
 src/intel/vulkan/genX_acceleration_structure.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/intel/vulkan/genX_acceleration_structure.c b/src/intel/vulkan/genX_acceleration_structure.c
index 8d8482bee3f..aed19064591 100644
--- a/src/intel/vulkan/genX_acceleration_structure.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/genX_acceleration_structure.c
@@ -324,7 +324,14 @@ get_bvh_layout(const struct vk_acceleration_structure_build_state *state,
       layout->leaf_block_map_offset = offset;
       offset += leaf_block_offset_size;
 
-      uint64_t parent_child_count_map_size = (leaf_count + internal_count) * sizeof(uint8_t);
+      /* Indexed by the internal node's block index (encode.comp/update.comp),
+       * and internal nodes and leaves share the block numbering, so this
+       * needs one entry per block like parent_child_map, not per internal
+       * node: sized by internal_count, encode wrote up to leaf_count bytes
+       * past the end of the acceleration structure.
+       */
+      uint64_t parent_child_count_map_size =
+         (internal_count + leaf_count + 1) * sizeof(uint8_t);
       layout->parent_child_count_map_offset = offset;
       offset += parent_child_count_map_size;
    }
